## Installation

### Method 1: Via `skills` package (recommended)

Requires [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) 18+ and the `skills` npm package (v1.5.12+).

```bash
npx skills install {{SKILL_AUTHOR}}/{{SKILL_NAME}}
```

### Method 2: Manual clone

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{SKILL_AUTHOR}}/{{SKILL_NAME}}.git ~/.claude/skills/{{SKILL_NAME}}
```

## Usage

After loading this skill, follow the workflow in [SKILL.md](SKILL.md).

## Distribution to other runtimes

```bash
bash <pangu>/scripts/gen-distribution.sh .
```

`<pangu>` = the pangu install directory (e.g. `~/.zcode/skills/pangu`). It generates two kinds of artifacts:

- **Isomorphic mirror**: `.trae/skills/{{SKILL_NAME}}` (or `.trae-cn` / `.codebuddy`), same directory layout as the native runtime, loads all references on demand
- **Condensed single file**: Cursor mdc / AGENTS.md / copilot-instructions, for runtimes without progressive disclosure

The condensed version keeps methods and gates complete, but reference details are summaries. Copy `references/` along when deeper detail is needed.

